### Changed

- Integrate the complete M9 Frontend Redesign milestone into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes at a single coherent release point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- Add inline citation badges to sanitized assistant Markdown, with numbered sources and hover or focus tooltips. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- Add a primary ticket action from the first actionable `SuggestedNextSteps` item, while keeping generic controls available as fallbacks. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- Add a keyboard-operable command palette to every page, opened with `Ctrl/Cmd+K`, with navigation entries and debounced, cancellable ticket search. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- Update ticket status optimistically on the board and detail view, then reconcile successful changes or restore the previous state when a change is rejected. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- Replace ticket status and assignee dialogs with inline popovers that apply changes through the existing command handlers. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- Add inline citation badges anchored to matching titles in assistant answers, with tooltips and a numbered sources list for citations without an anchor. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- Add the active agent roster to each chat system prompt and instruct the assistant to use roster names without inventing agents. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- Require `AgentLoop` to call `check_grounding` once after retrieval when no check has run, before streaming the answer. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- Centralize palette, spacing, radius, elevation, and semantic chip colors in `Theme/DesignTokens.cs`, and use the `KpiAccent` enum to specify tones for `KpiCard.Accent`. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- Wrap the board card title link so its two-line clamp with ellipsis applies without the grid item blockifying `-webkit-box`. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- Apply the assistant panel styles through `::deep .assistant-chat` so the composer stays inset within the panel. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- Set a `140px` width for the Category column and render its header with the uppercase label style to prevent overlap with Due. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- Add system-prompt rules requiring successful tool results before claiming a change and avoiding redundant confirmation when the user has requested a change. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- Convert ticket summary timestamps to the user timezone from `Anthropic:UserTimeZone` before including them in the model prompt. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- Return `IsError: true` for failed knowledge-base searches while keeping the unavailable path distinct and non-error. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- Score grounding with `SemanticGroundingEvaluator` using sentence-to-passage cosine similarity, with `LexicalGroundingEvaluator` as the fallback. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
